1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,100
This is the Moon, and we're rebuilding it from pure protons.

2
00:00:04,450 --> 00:00:06,500
Right now it's rock, made of atoms.

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:10,150
Each atom has protons in the middle, electrons around them.

4
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:14,200
Protons are positive, electrons negative, so they cancel out.

5
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:18,200
Now take away everything but the protons.

6
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:22,900
Nothing cancels, so every proton pushes on every other one.

7
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:29,100
Between two protons, that push beats gravity by a one with thirty-six zeros.

8
00:00:29,550 --> 00:00:31,600
A proton Moon couldn't hold together.

9
00:00:32,050 --> 00:00:33,500
It would blow itself apart.
